---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const grades=[['E0','Resemblance terminology only','The resemblance is recorded in the literature without an explicit mimicry claim or supporting data.'],['E1','Explicit author proposal','A cited author explicitly proposes the interaction as mimicry, without further support.'],['E2','Ecological, geographic or behavioral support','Distribution, seasonality or behavior is consistent with the proposed mimicry.'],['E3','Quantitative or experimental resemblance or receiver response','Measurements or experiments demonstrate the resemblance or a receiver response to it.'],['E4','Direct experimental biological outcome','Experiments demonstrate the biological outcome of the interaction for mimic or receiver.']];
---
<Layout><div class="container py-12"><h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Evidence grades</h1><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">Every record carries an evidence grade from the E0–E4 framework. Reporting a resemblance is not equivalent to demonstrating mimicry — the grade makes that distinction explicit. Curators record a reason and an evidence passage; grades are never assigned by keywords alone.</p><div class="mt-8 grid gap-4">{grades.map(([g,label,desc])=><div class="card flex gap-4"><span class="pill h-fit">{g}</span><div><div class="font-semibold">{label}</div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">{desc}</p></div></div>)}</div><p class="mt-8 text-sm text-slate-600">Full policy: <a href="https://github.com/ZyYang0124/MimicryDB/blob/main/docs/EVIDENCE_GUIDELINES.md">docs/EVIDENCE_GUIDELINES.md</a></p></div></Layout>
